pdoor:0:0:19:19:0:10:0:21:0:What is the name of the goddess who gave up her throne on Olympus to avoid conflict? the goddess who was offered the first sacrifice in every home and temple? the goddess who swore eternal virginity to remain neutral and focus on her duties? the goddess who protected orphans, refugees, and supplicants? the goddess who saved Poseidon’s son, Halirrhothios, from blasphemy? the goddess who maintained the “eternal flame” of Greek cities? the goddess who was so beloved that she never had myths of vengeance or cruelty? the goddess who shared her portion of offerings with the needy? the goddess who was worshipped alongside Hermes in doorways? the goddess who Rome adopted as Vesta, with priestesses (Vestals) guarding her flame?:hestia:0:silence.ogg:silence.ogg:win2.ogg:silence.ogg
