pdoor:0:0:40:40:0:10:0:42:0:who is the emperor who defeated Mark Antony and Cleopatra at the Battle of Actium (31 BCE)? the ruler who established the Pax Romana (Roman Peace), a 200-year era of stability? the emperor who reformed Rome’s tax system, built roads, and created a professional army? the leader who famously said, "I found Rome a city of bricks and left it a city of marble"? What is the name of Julius Caesar’s heir who avenged his death by defeating Caesar’s assassins (Brutus/Cassius)? the ruler whose death sparked the cult of the Divus Augustus (deified emperor)?:augustus:0:silence.ogg:silence.ogg:win2.ogg:silence.ogg
